WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.077
"And then Athena started yelling at Aphrodite."

2
00:00:05.078 --> 00:00:08.680
Brody's voice was shaky as he told his story.

3
00:00:08.681 --> 00:00:12.500
"I just put on my old chiton and sandals and got out of there."

4
00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:16.573
Julia had always seen Brody looking cocky and confident.

5
00:00:16.574 --> 00:00:20.581
But right now he seemed upset and unsure of himself.

6
00:00:20.582 --> 00:00:26.033
He'd come rushing out of the bath ten minutes earlier, babbling about almost being poisoned.

7
00:00:26.034 --> 00:00:34.548
She and Markos had led him to a private spot outside the gymnasium, where he'd told them the whole story of Aphrodite's visit.

8
00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:40.433
"Wow," Julia said. "And Athena mentioned Zeus' wife, Hera?"

9
00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:47.100
"Yeah," Brody said. "She seemed to think Aphrodite and Hera were working together or something."

10
00:00:47.101 --> 00:00:52.614
"That makes sense," Julia said, thinking back on the Greek myths she'd read.

11
00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:55.554
"I mean, it sounds like something Hera might do.

12
00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:59.741
It reminds me of the story about the Shirt of Nessus."

13
00:00:59.742 --> 00:01:03.071
"The shirt of what?" Brody looked blank.

14
00:01:03.072 --> 00:01:08.068
"Never mind, I'll tell you about it some other time," Julia said.

15
00:01:08.069 --> 00:01:11.843
"But what about trying to escape? Are you ready now?"

16
00:01:11.844 --> 00:01:17.901
Brody thought for a second. "Maybe," he said. "But how?"

17
00:01:17.902 --> 00:01:25.852
"We need to find a way to sneak into the Temple of Caerus." Julia glanced at Markos. "Will you help us?"

18
00:01:25.853 --> 00:01:32.613
She expected him to say no. To her surprise, however, Markos looked thoughtful.

19
00:01:32.614 --> 00:01:42.403
"Did Athena truly say that Hera and Aphrodite were working together?" he asked. "Because that would be quite unusual."

20
00:01:42.404 --> 00:01:48.297
"Why?" Brody said. "Wouldn't anyone want to work with Aphrodite?"

21
00:01:48.298 --> 00:01:56.124
Julia looked at him in astonishment. "She just tried to kill you, dummy! You can't still have a crush on her!"

22
00:01:56.125 --> 00:01:59.209
Looking unhappy, Brody shrugged.

23
00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:08.190
Markos looked troubled now. "Both Hermes and my father have ordered me to keep you safe," he told Brody.

24
00:02:08.191 --> 00:02:14.578
"But if Hera is after you, there is no safety for you in Olympia. Or anywhere in Greece, for that matter.

25
00:02:14.579 --> 00:02:19.733
Once Hera develops a grudge against someone, she won't stop until she's destroyed him."

26
00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:24.922
He shuddered. "Even Zeus himself is not always safe."

27
00:02:24.923 --> 00:02:30.647
"That's why we need to get home," Julia said. "Back to our own time."

28
00:02:30.648 --> 00:02:38.493
She looked at Markos. Would he help them? Or would he tell Hermes what they were planning?

29
00:02:38.494 --> 00:02:45.018
She and Brody had told Markos about the time passage in the temple on their first night in Greece.

30
00:02:45.019 --> 00:02:51.826
But Markos hadn't said much in response. Julia wasn't sure he believed they'd really come from the future.

31
00:02:51.827 --> 00:02:57.353
Finally Markos nodded. "I will try to help," he said.

32
00:02:57.354 --> 00:03:02.821
"In return, I ask only that you not tell Hermes that I did so.

33
00:03:02.822 --> 00:03:10.645
If he learns of my help, he will be angry and could even take out that anger on my father or the rest of my family."

34
00:03:10.646 --> 00:03:17.151
"Don't worry," Julia said. "Once we get out of here, we're planning never to see Hermes again.

35
00:03:17.152 --> 00:03:23.292
Now listen, I've been thinking about this, and I have some ideas about how we could get away. . ."

36
00:03:23.293 --> 00:03:33.317
The three of them spent the rest of the day concocting their plan. By dinnertime Julia was feeling confident. Hermes

37
00:03:33.318 --> 00:03:40.274
and Caerus entered the courtyard and took their seats at the table, just as they'd done the evening before. Julia

38
00:03:40.275 --> 00:03:46.279
watched from the doorway as Hermes started talking to Brody about his plans for training. Finally

39
00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:50.424
he turned away to talk with Markos' father. Julia

40
00:03:50.425 --> 00:03:55.833
hurried over to serve Brody a second helping of grilled fish. "You

41
00:03:55.834 --> 00:04:03.762
know what to do, right?" she whispered, glad for once that the girls and women of the household waited on the men and boys. Brody

42
00:04:03.763 --> 00:04:11.099
shoved some figs in his mouth. "You know, I'll miss some of this food," he mumbled. "Shh!"

43
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.887
Julia shot a worried look at Hermes. But

44
00:04:14.888 --> 00:04:24.822
Markos' father was telling a joke, and Hermes and Caerus were chuckling and paying no attention to Brody. Julia

45
00:04:24.823 --> 00:04:31.585
thought the meal would never end. But at last the two gods stood up from the table. "We

46
00:04:31.586 --> 00:04:36.224
must go," Hermes announced. He looked at Brody. "Be

47
00:04:36.225 --> 00:04:40.508
ready early tomorrow, my champion. We have much to do." "Okay,"

48
00:04:40.509 --> 00:04:43.265
Brody said. Julia

49
00:04:43.266 --> 00:04:51.574
was relieved. Hermes and Caerus always went to the agora to hang out with their god friends after dinner. She

50
00:04:51.575 --> 00:04:56.245
hoped they would stay away long enough for the kids' plan to work. "Oops!"

51
00:04:56.246 --> 00:05:01.139
she said, intentionally spilling water on Brody. "Hey!"

52
00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:08.423
Brody blustered. "Oh! I mean, um, I'd better change clothes." Julia

53
00:05:08.424 --> 00:05:15.889
glared at him. It was a good thing he was talented at football, because he wasn't much of an actor! Luckily

54
00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:23.115
Markos was much better. He turned to Julia. "Fetch us a dry chiton immediately." "Of

55
00:05:23.116 --> 00:05:28.458
course," Julia said. She rushed off. Moments

56
00:05:28.459 --> 00:05:32.207
later all three met outside the house. "That

57
00:05:32.208 --> 00:05:36.096
was pretty slick," Brody said with a grin. "Do

58
00:05:36.097 --> 00:05:38.865
you think we convinced your family, Markos?" Markos

59
00:05:38.866 --> 00:05:45.084
cast an anxious look at the house. "We should hurry," he said. "I'll

60
00:05:45.085 --> 00:05:48.005
be missed if I don't return soon." "You

61
00:05:48.006 --> 00:05:51.706
don't have to come with us," Julia told him. "It's

62
00:05:51.707 --> 00:05:55.209
not as if we'll get lost on the way to the temple." She

63
00:05:55.210 --> 00:06:02.858
gestured to the pale stone building, which was glowing in the moonlight above them. "We can see it from here." "It's

64
00:06:02.859 --> 00:06:09.052
all right," Markos said. "I should come along in case you run into any trouble." The

65
00:06:09.053 --> 00:06:12.683
three of them started for the path to the temple. Brody

66
00:06:12.684 --> 00:06:16.125
was in the lead as they rounded a turn. "Almost

67
00:06:16.126 --> 00:06:21.561
there," he said over his shoulder. "I think there's—ah!" He

68
00:06:21.562 --> 00:06:25.968
jumped back, startled, as something burst from a bush beside the trail. There

69
00:06:25.969 --> 00:06:29.776
was a flapping of wings and a loud caw !

70
00:06:29.777 --> 00:06:37.624
Brody laughed with relief. "Oh, man," he said. "It's just a bird."

71
00:06:37.625 --> 00:06:41.389
"A raven," Markos said, smiling.

72
00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.009
"Let's keep moving," Julia said, pushing ahead.

73
00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:48.480
"With any luck we should be there in less than—"

74
00:06:48.481 --> 00:06:54.723
She gasped as a tall form stepped out of the shadows just ahead.

75
00:06:54.724 --> 00:07:05.295
"Good evening, young mortals," Hera said. "Going somewhere?"

